2026-09-13  Christian Mauduit <ufoot@ufoot.org>

	* Version 0.3.1, Godot 4.7.2, pinned image tag in grcc.mk
	(GRCC_DOCKER_IMAGE), overridable Godot command and preset names,
	universal macOS dylib via lipo, native copy on arm64 Linux hosts.
	macOS SDK 26.1 (darwin25.1), NDK r29 and API level 24 (as Godot 4.7),
	llvm-mingw 20260908, bundletool 1.18.3, cmdline-tools 15859902,
	image installs the pinned wasm nightly used by grcc.mk.
	Base image Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute), JDK 17 only.
	Native amd64 and arm64 images tagged <version>-<arch>, selected by
	grcc.mk from the host (GRCC_DOCKER_ARCH). Android builds on arm64
	through NDK target files + distro clang/lld wrappers.
	Exports also build the Linux lib the in-image editor loads. Fixed
	toy export_presets.cfg numbering gap (Godot stops at first missing index).
	Android release signing via GODOT_ANDROID_KEYSTORE_RELEASE_* (default:
	image debug keystore); editor no longer runs x86 adb kill-server on exit.
	osxcross pinned, "llvm" flavor (distro clang + ld64.lld), build failures
	no longer hidden by tee; SDKROOT set for rustc.
	Toy project imports both S3TC/BPTC and ETC2/ASTC (exports from either arch).
	Toy crates enable godot experimental-wasm, required for any wasm build.
	Windows installers: makensis -NOCD so project-relative paths resolve.
	Image builds libdmg-hfsplus (Mozilla fork) for grcc-dmg-macosx, which
	now calls "dmg dmg".
	Entrypoint (tini + entrypoint.sh) gives root-owned files under /build
	back to the host user on Linux.
	grcc-pkg-android-aab / grcc-sign-android-aab: unsigned Gradle AAB for
	Google Play, validated with bundletool, then upload-key signature
	(amd64 image only); toy "Android AAB" preset.
	Signing keys read from .keystore/ (release key when its password is in
	the environment, else project debug key); excluded from source packages.
	grcc-pkg-source also excludes *.keystore/*.jks, target/ caches and the
	Gradle template, and fails if a key file still ends up in the archive.
	On arm64 hosts the AAB export runs in the emulated amd64 image by default
	(GRCC_AAB_EMULATE=no to skip); explicit notice when no AAB is built.
	Gradle daemon disabled for AAB exports. CI split into one job per
	platform (a single export job exceeds the 30 GB GitLab.com runner disk).
	Projects share grcc.mk and .gitlab/ci/grcc.yml (GitLab CI template, included
	locally) with thin Makefile/.gitlab-ci.yml wrappers: new grcc-lint*,
	grcc-format*, grcc-build, grcc-sync, grcc-ci-restore-android-keystores
	targets, GRCC_ALIASES short names; toy passes clippy -D warnings, rustfmt
	and gdtoolkit.
	CI export-web runs on saas-linux-medium-amd64 (OOM on the 8 GB runner);
	grcc-check-android-signing opens the release keystore with keytool.

